I'm pretty sure you mistook "displacing your pet
into a trap" for "displacing your pet, at all". If
merely displacing pets _at all_ (which I tend to do
more often than once per dozen turns) caused
negative alignment hits, I'd _never_ get prayers
answered, and such is not the case.

On the other hand, pets _do_ have a modest effect on
alignment, sometimes pro, sometimes con, just
because if the pet kills a monster, you don't get an
alignment hit or bonus, as appropriate to the
killing of that monster done yourself. Pets killing
peacefuls so I don't have to take the bad joss that
goes with such behavior is probably at least number
three on my all time hit parade "why I like pets"
list.

